st listed study-room display.","evidence_claim":"Georgetown lists the Millennium Room as its largest Hilltop group study room, accommodating up to ten people and providing a 50-inch LCD display.","source_url":"https://library.georgetown.edu/carrels-lockers-space/group-study","source_title":"Group Study Rooms","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Advance reservations are limited to eligible Hilltop community members. Rooms are booked in one-hour segments, and a reservation is forfeited after 15 minutes if the group has not arrived.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"georgetown-duran-visualization-learning-lab","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Duran Visualization and Learning Lab","title":"Scale Up a Data-Heavy Research Session","subtitle":"A technology-enabled lab inside Pierce Reading Room","notes":"Use this lab for computational or visualization work only after confirming eligibility and securing the required reservation.","short_summary":"A specialized environment for research teams working with computation, data, and large-scale visualization.","evidence_claim":"Georgetown describes the Duran Visualization and Learning Lab as a technology-enabled space reservable for instructional sessions or computational and data-intensive research and visualization.","source_url":"https://library.georgetown.edu/study-spaces/pierce","source_title":"Pierce Reading Room","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Inside Pierce Reading Room on Lauinger's third floor. Faculty, staff, and research teams may reserve it; student requests are evaluated case by case.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
